DevOps Engineer

Job Title: DevOps Engineer
Experience: 2–5 Years
Employment Type: Full-Time

Job Description

We are looking for a DevOps Engineer to automate software delivery, infrastructure provisioning, deployment, monitoring, and operational processes. The ideal candidate should have experience with cloud platforms, CI/CD, containers, and infrastructure automation.

Responsibilities
Design, implement, and maintain CI/CD pipelines.
Automate application build, testing, deployment, and release processes.
Manage cloud infrastructure and production environments.
Deploy and manage containerized applications using Docker and Kubernetes.
Implement Infrastructure as Code using Terraform or equivalent tools.
Monitor application and infrastructure performance.
Configure logging, alerting, and observability solutions.
Troubleshoot deployment, infrastructure, networking, and production issues.
Implement security and access-control best practices.
Collaborate with software engineers to improve deployment reliability.
Automate repetitive operational tasks.
Support disaster recovery, scalability, and high-availability initiatives.
Required Skills
Experience with AWS, Azure, or GCP.
Strong knowledge of Linux.
Experience with Docker.
Hands-on experience with Kubernetes.
Experience building CI/CD pipelines using Jenkins, GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, or similar.
Knowledge of Terraform or Infrastructure as Code.
Strong understanding of Git.
Knowledge of networking, DNS, HTTP/HTTPS, and security fundamentals.
Experience with monitoring and logging tools.
Scripting knowledge using Bash, Python, or similar.
Preferred Skills
Helm.
Ansible.
Prometheus and Grafana.
ELK/OpenSearch.
AWS services such as EC2, S3, ECS/EKS, RDS, Lambda, and CloudWatch.
DevSecOps practices.